<title>ITALY: Italian treasury to issue euro-denominated bond.</title>
<headline>Italian treasury to issue euro-denominated bond.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The treasury said the Republic of Italy intended to issue a seven-year one billion Euro-denominated bond.</p>
<p>Bank Paribas and SBC Warburg will act as joint bookrunners for the issue, the treasury said. Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
